AgentCoin licensing (decision D47)
==================================

AgentCoin is licensed by directory. Reusable libraries are permissive so that
wallets, SDKs and other chains can embed them; programs, services, tests and
scripts are copyleft.

| Zone       | Directories                                                      | SPDX expression      |
|------------|------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------|
| GPL        | node/ (including node/consensus/*), services/,                   | GPL-3.0-or-later     |
|            | clients/wallet-cli/, tests/, scripts/                            |                      |
| Permissive | everything else, including crates/, pallets/, runtime/, docs/,   | MIT OR Apache-2.0    |
|            | openspec/, the repository root and any new directory             |                      |

- Permissive zone: you may use it under either the MIT licence (LICENSE-MIT)
  or the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE), at your option.
- GPL zone: GNU General Public License v3.0 or (at your option) any later
  version (LICENSE-GPL).
- Each Cargo package declares its zone's expression in its `license` field,
  each Python package in its `pyproject.toml` `project.license`;
  `scripts/check-license-boundary.sh` enforces the zones in CI.
- Third-party snapshots keep their upstream licence
  (docs/rust-guidelines/ is MIT, see its own notice).
- Internal features: the zones apply to what can be distributed. A few Cargo
  features are internal (registered in scripts/check-license-boundary.sh;
  today only `runtime-benchmarks`) and may pull in registered GPL-only
  dependencies (today only `pallet-revive-fixtures`, GPL-3.0-only, the
  upstream benchmark contracts). AgentCoin never distributes builds with an
  internal feature enabled, and CI checks that the release runtime exposes no
  benchmarking API. If you build with an internal feature and distribute the
  result, that result is subject to the GPL.

Contributions: a contribution to a directory is licensed under that
directory's licence (inbound = outbound). There is no separate CLA.

Earlier versions: commits made before this licence split (up to and including
commit 117712b) were released under the MIT licence alone and remain
available under it.

